LS (advanced trauma life support) in Switzerland]</article-title><source>Swiss Surg</source><year>2000</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>343</fpage><lpage>346</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11142159</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1024/1023-9332.6.6.343</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rastad</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Lindebert</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>["Advanced trauma life support" in Sweden. A flying start for trauma education]</article-title><source>Lakartidningen</source><year>1996</year><volume>93</volume><fpage>2660</fpage><lpage>2661</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8765782</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Skinner</surname><given-names>DV</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Advanced trauma life support</article-title><source>Injury</source><year>1993</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>147</fpage><lpage>148</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8509178</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0020-1383(93)90277-D</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kortbeek</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name><name><surname>Al Turki</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Ali</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Antoine</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Bouillon</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Brasel</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Brenneman</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Brink</surname><given-names>PR</given-names></name><name><surname>Brohi</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Burris</surname><given-names>D</given-names></nam